---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Newsletter · Informal Engineer"
  description="Lab Notes weekly: what got tested, what the numbers said, one useful link. Under 500 words."
>
  <h1>Lab Notes, weekly</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    One email a week: the week's lab notes with a line of context each, and
    one link to something I genuinely used. Under 500 words, plain text
    energy, no growth hacks.
  </p>

  <p class="section-label">a note on the transition</p>
  <p class="lede">
    This list used to be called Founder Design Handbook on the old site. Same
    author, new name, sharper focus (builds and numbers instead of everything
    at once). If you were subscribed there, you'll get one re-introduction
    email with a very easy unsubscribe link, no hard feelings either way.
  </p>

  <p class="section-label">subscribe</p>
  <p class="lede">
    The new sending setup is going live right now. Until the form exists,
    subscribing is one honest email:
  </p>
  <a
    href="mailto:MeshaelR@gmail.com?subject=Subscribe%20to%20Lab%20Notes&body=Sign%20me%20up."
    style="display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: #101214; padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500;"
  >
    Subscribe by email
  </a>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
    Prefer a reader? The <a href="/rss.xml">full-content RSS feed</a> carries
    everything the email does.
  </p>
</Base>
